    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633-a1">

                <pb facs="0748" n="706" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg706"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 27, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received yours of the 20th instant,
                    covering copy of despatch of Lord Lyons of the 19th, relative to the detention
                    of the steamer Josie by the custom-house authorities at New York.</p>
                <p>This despatch was sent by me on, the 21st to the collector at New York for a
                    report on the case, a copy of which I enclose.</p>
                <p>With great respect,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. P. CHASE, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Treasury.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
